  "description": "Beetle (Coleoptera) records in GBIF from three Swedish provinces in 2024, counted per species. Statistics idea: a species count depends on effort. Rarefaction (Hurlbert's formula, from the binomial coefficients as lgamma) gives the species expected in a random subsample of n records, so provinces compare at equal effort; Chao1 estimates how many species exist from those seen once and twice, and singletons / records is the chance the next record is a new species. Caveats: GBIF records are not a random sample (surveys are clumped, observers chase rarities, provinces differ in size and habitat), and Chao1 is a lower bound.",
